<title>UK: NW Europe oil, gas rigs up four in week - Andersen.</title>
<headline>NW Europe oil, gas rigs up four in week - Andersen.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe rose by four rigs to 61 in the week to October 30, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>There were 28 rigs active in U.K. waters, up two, and the Norwegian total rose by one to 19 rigs.</p>
<p>In the Dutch sector, there were 10 rigs active, up two on the week, while Irish activity was steady at one rig. There were three rigs active in Danish waters, down one, Andersen said.</p>
<p>Onshore drilling activity in the U.K. slipped a rig to three but was steady at one rig in the Faroe Islands.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
